{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have strong evidence that Isobel Maddison is a scholar of Elizabeth von Arnim (an English writer), with a 2012 article in First World War Studies. The Wikipedia article on Elizabeth von Arnim confirms she was an English novelist, and Isobel Maddison is listed as a scholar who has published on von Arnim. However, I have not been able to verify the specific remaining clues: the Routledge 2018 co-edited book, the research group founded in 2009 (coordinator as of December 2023), the panel convenor role, and the PhD completion. The searches have become repetitive without new evidence.\n\nGiven the strong convergence of evidence on Isobel Maddison as a scholar of Elizabeth von Arnim (an English writer) with a 2012 publication, but lacking verification of the other specific clues (Routledge 2018 co-edited book, research group founded 2009, panel convenor, PhD), I should abstain rather than guess.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"abstain\": true, \"reason\": \"The strongest candidate is Isobel Maddison, a scholar of Elizabeth von Arnim (an English writer), with a 2012 article in First World War Studies (per Wikipedia's Elizabeth von Arnim article, e1/e2). However, I could not verify the remaining required clues: (1) a Routledge 2018 co-edited book, (2) coordinator of a research group founded in 2009 as of December 2023, (3) panel convenor before 2020, and (4) completion of a PhD on von Arnim's writings. Searches became repetitive without locating her academic profile page or the specific Routledge 2018 volume. Without verification of these distinguishing clues, I cannot confidently confirm the answer.\"}","name":"finish"},"id":"call_97e94de3fac4408ca4208c1b","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789481228,"id":"chatcmpl-f10151b9-50e9-9d89-933b-577b901ed152","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":21777,"completion_tokens":369,"reasoni